WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.761 --> 00:00:13.769
One summer a young grasshopper moved into a forest.

2
00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:16.911
"What a beautiful place!"

3
00:00:17.511 --> 00:00:18.072
he thought.

4
00:00:18.092 --> 00:00:20.093
"I'll live here."

5
00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.575
The happy grasshopper did a little dance.

6
00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:29.820
Soon a group of ants marched by, carrying green leaves and grass.

7
00:00:31.416 --> 00:00:32.417
"Hello, new neighbors!"

8
00:00:33.857 --> 00:00:34.878
Grasshopper waved.

9
00:00:34.898 --> 00:00:38.360
"Would you like to play with me?"

10
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.822
"We're busy today," the ants said.

11
00:00:41.842 --> 00:00:44.563
"We don't have time to play."

12
00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:48.105
"Come on!"

13
00:00:48.525 --> 00:00:49.446
Grasshopper said.

14
00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:52.127
"It's a beautiful day.

15
00:00:53.168 --> 00:00:54.849
We'll have so much fun."

16
00:00:54.869 --> 00:00:58.871
"Sorry," the ants said before marching away.

17
00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:06.385
The next day Grasshopper woke up late.

18
00:01:07.945 --> 00:01:09.566
He saw the ants marching by again.

19
00:01:09.586 --> 00:01:12.366
"Hi there, neighbors!"

20
00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:13.267
he said.

21
00:01:17.168 --> 00:01:18.608
are you out so early?"

22
00:01:18.628 --> 00:01:23.050
"It's not early," one ant said.

23
00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:26.311
"We're working," another said.

24
00:01:26.331 --> 00:01:29.271
"Why do you need to work so much?"

25
00:01:29.812 --> 00:01:30.912
Grasshopper asked.

26
00:01:32.632 --> 00:01:35.894
"We're gathering food for winter," a little ant said.

27
00:01:35.914 --> 00:01:43.958
"Winter?" Grasshopper laughed.

28
00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:47.320
"It's summer!

29
00:01:50.201 --> 00:01:52.863
It's too early to get ready for winter!

30
00:01:52.883 --> 00:01:55.584
How foolish!"

31
00:01:55.604 --> 00:01:58.746
"You're foolish!"

32
00:01:59.166 --> 00:01:59.847
an ant said.

33
00:01:59.867 --> 00:02:03.805
"Why?" Grasshopper asked.

34
00:02:03.825 --> 00:02:08.629
"You'll see," the ant warned him.

35
00:02:14.173 --> 00:02:17.696
As summer passed, Grasshopper spent each day having fun.

36
00:02:21.559 --> 00:02:22.520
He slept late.

37
00:02:26.403 --> 00:02:27.604
Then he danced and played.

38
00:02:32.636 --> 00:02:36.639
"You work too much," Grasshopper said whenever the ants went by.

39
00:02:36.659 --> 00:02:40.802
"You play too much," the ants said.

40
00:02:46.326 --> 00:02:49.228
Soon fall arrived, and the forest changed colors.

41
00:02:50.909 --> 00:02:53.992
Leaves fell from trees, and the grass turned brown.

42
00:02:55.152 --> 00:02:59.195
Grasshopper still played every day, and the ants were busier than ever.

43
00:03:04.644 --> 00:03:07.747
One morning Grasshopper woke up, feeling cold.

44
00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:11.991
When he opened his eyes, he saw it was snowing.

45
00:03:13.153 --> 00:03:16.336
Snow covered the ground, and all the trees were bare.

46
00:03:21.221 --> 00:03:22.502
Grasshopper shivered.

47
00:03:22.522 --> 00:03:25.485
"Winter is here.

48
00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:28.428
I should look for food."

49
00:03:32.352 --> 00:03:36.015
Grasshopper searched the snowy forest but couldn't find anything to eat.

50
00:03:38.716 --> 00:03:41.999
The next day Grasshopper still couldn't find any food.

51
00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:45.161
He searched long and hard.

52
00:03:46.542 --> 00:03:48.903
Eventually he found the ants' home.

53
00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:58.209
Grasshopper begged.

54
00:03:58.229 --> 00:04:00.831
"Where can I find food?

55
00:04:03.344 --> 00:04:05.545
I'm so hungry!"

56
00:04:05.565 --> 00:04:09.546
"It's too late," one ant said.

57
00:04:10.966 --> 00:04:11.766
Another nodded.

58
00:04:11.786 --> 00:04:15.307
"You won't find any food until spring."

59
00:04:16.668 --> 00:04:17.928
"What will I do?"

60
00:04:23.169 --> 00:04:24.370
Grasshopper sobbed.

61
00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.531
The little ant looked at the other ants.

62
00:04:28.551 --> 00:04:32.172
"Grasshopper will die without food."

63
00:04:33.984 --> 00:04:35.064
The others sighed.

64
00:04:35.084 --> 00:04:39.586
"Fine," one said.

65
00:04:39.606 --> 00:04:42.186
"There is only one thing to do."

66
00:04:43.867 --> 00:04:46.487
That winter Grasshopper stayed with the ants.

67
00:04:49.768 --> 00:04:51.089
They shared their food with him.

68
00:04:53.689 --> 00:04:58.411
Grasshopper was thankful for their kindness, and he learned an important lesson.

69
00:05:02.352 --> 00:05:05.678
As soon as spring arrived, Grasshopper darted outside.

70
00:05:05.698 --> 00:05:08.320
"Where are you going?"

71
00:05:08.661 --> 00:05:09.842
the little ant asked.

72
00:05:11.123 --> 00:05:12.605
Grasshopper smiled.

73
00:05:12.625 --> 00:05:15.207
"I have work to do.

74
00:05:15.227 --> 00:05:18.230
I must gather food for winter!"
